  "question": {
    "text": "Let the ratio of the fifth term from the beginning to the fifth term from the end in the binomial expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mroot><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></math>, in the increasing powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mroot><mn>6</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If the sixth term from the beginning is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "84",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>The ratio of the fifth term from the beginning to the fifth term from the end in the binomial expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mroot><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;in the increasing powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mroot><mn>6</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now according to given data we have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mroot><mn>6</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>84</mn><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></math></p><p>Now comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mroot><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mroot></mfrac></math>,</p><p>We get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
